{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Tensor Operations Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The code lives in `code/tensors.py`. Each step references the implementation there."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Tensor storage and strides"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A tensor stores a flat list of numbers plus shape metadata. Strides tell the indexing logic how to map multi-dimensional indices to flat positions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Tensor:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, data, shape=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if isinstance(data, (list, tuple)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self._data, self._shape = self._flatten_nested(data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif isinstance(data, np.ndarray):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self._data = data.flatten().tolist()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self._shape = tuple(data.shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self._data = [data]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self._shape = ()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if shape is not None:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            total = reduce(lambda a, b: a * b, shape, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if total != len(self._data):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                raise ValueError("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    f\"Cannot reshape {len(self._data)} elements into shape {shape}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self._shape = tuple(shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self._strides = self._compute_strides(self._shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    @staticmethod"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _compute_strides(shape):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if len(shape) == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return ()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        strides = [1] * len(shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(len(shape) - 2, -1, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            strides[i] = strides[i + 1] * shape[i + 1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return tuple(strides)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For shape `(3, 4)`, strides are `(4, 1)` -- skip 4 elements to advance one row, skip 1 element to advance one column."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Reshape, squeeze, unsqueeze"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Reshape changes the shape without changing element order. The total number of elements must stay the same. Use `-1` for one dimension to infer its size."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "t = Tensor(list(range(12)), shape=(2, 6))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "r = t.reshape((3, 4))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "r = t.reshape((-1, 3))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Squeeze removes axes of size 1. Unsqueeze inserts one. Unsqueezing is critical for broadcasting -- a bias vector `(D,)` added to a batch `(B, T, D)` needs unsqueezing to `(1, 1, D)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "t = Tensor(list(range(6)), shape=(1, 3, 1, 2))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "s = t.squeeze()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "v = Tensor([1, 2, 3])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "u = v.unsqueeze(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Transpose and permute"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Transpose swaps two axes. Permute reorders all axes. This is how you convert between NCHW and NHWC."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "mat = Tensor(list(range(6)), shape=(2, 3))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tr = mat.transpose(0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "t4d = Tensor(list(range(24)), shape=(1, 2, 3, 4))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "perm = t4d.permute((0, 2, 3, 1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "After transpose or permute, the tensor is non-contiguous in memory. In PyTorch, `view` fails on non-contiguous tensors -- use `reshape` or call `.contiguous()` first."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Element-wise operations and reductions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Element-wise ops (add, multiply, subtract) apply independently to each element and preserve shape. Reductions (sum, mean, max) collapse one or more axes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "a = Tensor([[1, 2], [3, 4]])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "b = Tensor([[10, 20], [30, 40]])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "c = a + b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "d = a * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "s = a.sum(axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Global average pooling in a CNN: `(B, C, H, W).mean(axis=[2, 3])` produces `(B, C)`. Sequence mean pooling in NLP: `(B, T, D).mean(axis=1)` produces `(B, D)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Broadcasting with NumPy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `demo_broadcasting_numpy()` function in `tensors.py` shows the core patterns."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "activations = np.random.randn(4, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "bias = np.array([0.1, 0.2, 0.3])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result = activations + bias"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "images = np.random.randn(2, 3, 4, 4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "scale = np.array([0.5, 1.0, 1.5]).reshape(1, 3, 1, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result = images * scale"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "a = np.array([1, 2, 3]).reshape(-1, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "b = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "outer = a * b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Pairwise distance via broadcasting: reshape `(M, 2)` to `(M, 1, 2)` and `(N, 2)` to `(1, N, 2)`, subtract, square, sum along last axis, take square root. Result: `(M, N)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Einsum operations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `demo_einsum()` and `demo_einsum_gallery()` functions walk through every common pattern."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "a = np.array([1.0, 2.0, 3.0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "b = np.array([4.0, 5.0, 6.0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "dot = np.einsum(\"i,i->\", a, b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]], dtype=float)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "B = np.array([[7, 8, 9], [10, 11, 12]], dtype=float)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "matmul = np.einsum(\"ik,kj->ij\", A, B)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "batch_A = np.random.randn(4, 3, 5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "batch_B = np.random.randn(4, 5, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "batch_mm = np.einsum(\"bij,bjk->bik\", batch_A, batch_B)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The computational cost of a contraction is the product of all index sizes (kept and summed). For `bij,bjk->bik` with B=32, I=128, J=64, K=128: `32 * 128 * 64 * 128 = 33,554,432` multiply-adds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Attention mechanism via einsum"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `demo_attention_einsum()` function implements multi-head attention end to end."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "B, H, T, D = 2, 4, 8, 16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "E = H * D"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X = np.random.randn(B, T, E)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "W_q = np.random.randn(E, E) * 0.02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Q = np.einsum(\"bte,ek->btk\", X, W_q)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Q = Q.reshape(B, T, H, D).transpose(0, 2, 1, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "scores = np.einsum(\"bhtd,bhsd->bhts\", Q, K) / np.sqrt(D)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "weights = softmax(scores, axis=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "attn_output = np.einsum(\"bhts,bhsd->bhtd\", weights, V)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "concat = attn_output.transpose(0, 2, 1, 3).reshape(B, T, E)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "output = np.einsum(\"bte,ek->btk\", concat, W_o)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Every step is a tensor operation: projection (matmul via einsum), head splitting (reshape + transpose), attention scores (batch matmul via einsum), weighted sum (batch matmul via einsum), head merging (transpose + reshape), output projection (matmul via einsum)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy -- Reshape round-trip.** Take a tensor of shape `(2, 3, 4)`. Reshape it to `(6, 4)`, then to `(24,)`, then back to `(2, 3, 4)`. Verify element order is preserved at each step by printing the flat data.\n\n2. **Medium -- Implement broadcasting.** Extend the `Tensor` class with a `broadcast_to(shape)` method that expands dimensions of size 1 to match a target shape. Then modify `_elementwise_op` to automatically broadcast before operating. Test with shapes `(3, 1)` and `(1, 4)` producing `(3, 4)`.\n\n3. **Hard -- Build einsum from scratch.** Implement a basic `einsum(subscripts, *tensors)` function that handles at least: dot product (`i,i->`), matrix multiply (`ij,jk->ik`), outer product (`i,j->ij`), and transpose (`ij->ji`). Parse the subscript string, identify contracted indices, and loop over all index combinations. Compare your results against `np.einsum`.\n\n4. **Hard -- Attention shape tracker.** Write a function that takes `batch_size`, `seq_len`, `embed_dim`, and `num_heads` as inputs and prints the exact shape at every step of multi-head attention: input, Q/K/V projection, head split, attention scores, softmax weights, weighted sum, head merge, output projection. Verify against the `demo_attention_einsum()` output."
      ]
    }
  ],
